course: dictionary
lesson: 11996
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word char is one of them, and the sentence around it tells you which meaning is right. Look for clues such as cooking, cleaning, tea or fish.
explain: «Dad let the sausages char on the barbecue until their skins went black.» Here char means to burn a little, so the outside turns black. The clues are barbecue and black.
explain: «The char came every Tuesday to clean the old house.» In old British stories, a char is a cleaning woman who is paid to clean houses or offices. Old-fashioned words like this often appear in books set long ago.
explain: «Grandma put the kettle on and made us a cup of char.» In informal British English, char means tea. The Arctic char is a different meaning altogether: a fish that lives in cold water. Always check the whole sentence before you choose a meaning.
fact: Char can be a verb (to char, charred, charring) or a noun (char).
fact: «Char» means to burn something a little so the outside goes black.
fact: «Char» means a cleaning woman in old British English, short for charwoman.
fact: «Char» means tea in informal British English, as in «a cup of char».
fact: The Arctic char is a fish that lives in cold lakes and seas, and it is related to trout and salmon.
exercise: «The sausages were charred on the barbecue.» What does charred mean here? | Frozen solid | *Burnt a little, with black marks | Washed clean | Cooked in cold water
exercise: «The char arrived early to clean the office.» What is a char in this sentence? | A small wooden boat | A fish from a cold lake | A type of bread | *A cleaning woman paid to clean
exercise: «Would you like a cup of char?» In this sentence, char means | Soup | Smoke from a fire | A cleaning job | *Tea
test: «The Arctic char swam slowly under the ice of the cold lake.» What kind of thing is the Arctic char? | A kind of bread | *A fish | A black mark on paper | A cleaning woman
test: «The old wooden beams were charred black after the fire.» What does charred mean here? | Soaked in water for a week | *Burnt a little, so the outside is black | Painted bright blue | Made very smooth and shiny
exam: Which meaning of char fits best in «The char who cleans our school arrives at seven each morning»? | *A cleaning woman paid to clean | Burnt wood | Tea | Cold-water fish
